WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.067
-Welcome back, everybody!

00:00:02.067 --> 00:00:03.667
We are hanging out
with Samuel L. Jackson!

00:00:03.667 --> 00:00:06.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:06.234 --> 00:00:09.100
We want to talk about
your new Apple TV+ show,

00:00:09.100 --> 00:00:11.934
"The Last Days of Ptolemy Grey."
-Mm.

00:00:11.934 --> 00:00:14.801
-You had the rights to this
12 years ago?

00:00:14.801 --> 00:00:17.601
-Yeah, 10, 12 years, yeah.
-Took you 12 years to make this?

00:00:17.601 --> 00:00:20.601
-Well, you know...
I was trying to get

00:00:20.601 --> 00:00:23.400
the ordinary people who were
doing, like, streamer --

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.000
Well, not streamers,
but series and stuff to do it,

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.667
and they were like,
"Well, you know,

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.367
let's just see if we can
make a movie out of it."

00:00:29.367 --> 00:00:31.033
And they wanted to do it
an hour and a half, two hours.

00:00:31.033 --> 00:00:33.234
The book's kind of
too deep to do that.

00:00:33.234 --> 00:00:36.501
So I was very resistant,
but I had let them

00:00:36.501 --> 00:00:38.701
buy the rights from me,
so I had to wait until

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:41.234
everything went into turnaround
so I could get it back...

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.300
-Yeah.
Oh, my God.

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.834
-...and get it done
somewhere else.

00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:45.601
But, you know, things happen
when they're supposed to,

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:47.334
so in the time of streaming,
it's perfect.

00:00:47.334 --> 00:00:48.834
-Yeah.
-So I'm happy.

00:00:48.834 --> 00:00:50.834
-How many parts is it?
-Six.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:53.367
-Six parts.
-So, Friday, there'll be

00:00:53.367 --> 00:00:56.267
episode 1 and 2,
and then, every Friday

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.968
for the next four weeks,
you'll get the rest of it.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:01.000
-And what was it about the book
that connected you so much?

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.934
-Well, Ptolemy is --
Ptolemy's a 92-, 93-year-old man

00:01:04.934 --> 00:01:07.567
who's suffering
from Alzheimer's dementia.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:11.634
And my grandfather, my mom,
her brother, her sister,

00:01:11.634 --> 00:01:13.868
and my father's sister
all had it.

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:15.701
-Oof.
-So, I kind of watched the light

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.501
go out in a lot
of people's eyes.

00:01:17.501 --> 00:01:20.300
And the story is beautiful.

00:01:20.300 --> 00:01:23.701
And this guy is isolated.

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:27.267
The kid that takes care of him
gets killed in a drive-by.

00:01:27.267 --> 00:01:29.734
That's not a big secret,
that's not a plot divulge.

00:01:29.734 --> 00:01:33.934
And he's by himself until this
17-year-old girl happens to --

00:01:33.934 --> 00:01:35.100
-Who is amazing.
Dominique Fishback.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.567
-Dominique Fishback
happens to come by.

00:01:37.567 --> 00:01:41.434
And they end up having
this beautiful relationship,

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:45.601
where she's been taking care of
her mom, who was an addict

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.133
for a long time, who died.

00:01:47.133 --> 00:01:52.567
And she's never had really love
or been able to act like a kid.

00:01:52.567 --> 00:01:55.501
He has a doctor's appointment
she takes him to,

00:01:55.501 --> 00:01:57.901
where this guy proposes to him,
"I have this drug

00:01:57.901 --> 00:02:01.767
that will allow you to be clear
for a specific amount of time,

00:02:01.767 --> 00:02:03.834
and then it's gonna kill you.

00:02:03.834 --> 00:02:06.167
But it's up to you
to make up your mind

00:02:06.167 --> 00:02:07.634
if you're gonna take it."
So you're asking a dude

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:09.267
with dementia,
does he want to take a drug.

00:02:09.267 --> 00:02:11.267
You know, she's like,
"How's that work?"

00:02:11.267 --> 00:02:13.834
And he has to make that choice.

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.100
And it's, you know,
you follow --

00:02:16.100 --> 00:02:18.767
you go back in his life
and see a life well-lived.

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:20.000
-It's well done...
-And, you know, totally cool.

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.067
-...and it's beautiful,
and it's very, very cool.

00:02:22.067 --> 00:02:23.434
-Yeah, nice little mystery
in there.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:25.868
-Yeah, exactly right.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:02:25.868 --> 00:02:29.033
Here's Samuel L. Jackson in
"The Last Days of Ptolemy Grey."

00:02:29.033 --> 00:02:31.934
Take a look at this.

00:02:31.934 --> 00:02:35.133
-That in there ain't right.
-Oh, well, stop -- stop --

00:02:35.133 --> 00:02:36.801
stop doing what you're doing
and go close that door.

00:02:36.801 --> 00:02:38.267
-No, no, no, no.
You listen!

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.133
That's don't get dealt with,
I'mma be haunted.

00:02:40.133 --> 00:02:41.834
You understand?
Haunted.

00:02:41.834 --> 00:02:43.167
-Mnh, mnh, mnh.
-Mm-hmm.

00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.601
So where your cleaning stuff at?
-My treasures.

00:02:44.601 --> 00:02:46.601
Unh-unh, unh-unh.
-What are you talking about?

00:02:46.601 --> 00:02:49.400
-Every time Reggie said he gonna
clean up here and here,

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:52.234
he end up throwing away all --
all my best things.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:53.868
My best things!
-Oh, yeah? Like what?

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:56.634
-[ Stammers ]

00:02:56.634 --> 00:02:58.100
[ Groans ]
-Oh, come on.

00:02:58.100 --> 00:03:00.133
Don't do that.

00:03:00.133 --> 00:03:02.701
Come on.
I'll show you.

00:03:02.701 --> 00:03:04.834
-Oh, you're moving too fast!
-Oh, I'm sorry.

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:07.033
Here, sit, sit.
Sorry.

00:03:07.033 --> 00:03:10.167
-[ Panting ]

00:03:10.167 --> 00:03:11.801
-I'll tell you what.

00:03:11.801 --> 00:03:13.701
I'll show you everything
before I toss it.

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.534
You get to decide.
-Huh?

00:03:15.534 --> 00:03:17.267
-You like that?
-Uh, uh...

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.100
-Yeah, yeah, yeah,
you like that.

00:03:19.100 --> 00:03:21.567
-Yeah, that's right.
Samuel L. Jackson, everybody.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:24.100
"The Last Days of Ptolemy Grey"

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:27.133
begins streaming this Friday
on Apple TV+.

